# Line endings.
#
# This repository targets Linux. Every text file must be stored with LF line endings, on
# every platform, because the artifacts are copied verbatim into a Debian chroot:
#
#   * a shell script or hook with CRLF fails at run time with `\r: not found`, or worse,
#     silently breaks a `case`/`esac` pattern in a #!/bin/sh hook;
#   * /etc/fstab, /etc/hosts and the GRUB configuration dislike trailing carriage returns;
#   * dpkg maintainer scripts are run by sh, not bash, and are strict about this.
#
# `eol=lf` keeps the working copy LF too, so a build run directly from a Windows checkout
# behaves the same as one run from the committed tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched by the text normalisation above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.xz binary
*.gz binary
*.zst binary
*.deb binary

# The ISO and its sidecars are build output; keep them out of diffs.
*.iso binary
*.squashfs binary
*.img binary
